-- title:
--   Kronecker congruence in subrings: (j^q-j_q)(j-j_q^q)∈ qR
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number carrying a `Fact` instance that it is prime, and let $R$ be a subring of the field of Laurent series $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, that is, of Hahn series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with value group $\mathbb{Z}$. Two elements of this Laurent series field are involved: `jqModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, the product of the Hahn monomial $\mathfrak q^{-1}$ with the image of the integral power series $\mathtt{jNum} = E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-\text{unit}}$ (the numerator power series $E_4^3$ times the inverse unit coming from the Dedekind eta expansion) pushed into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. the $\mathfrak q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$; and `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (1 * q)`, the image of the former under the ring homomorphism `qExpand` which rescales exponents by the factor $1\cdot q$, i.e. the expansion $j(\mathfrak q^{q})$. The hypotheses `hj` and `hjq` assert that these two Laurent series belong to $R$; write $J$ and $J_q$ for the corresponding elements of the subring. The conclusion is that the product $(J^{q}-J_q)\,(J-J_q^{\,q})$ lies in the ideal of $R$ generated by the image of the natural number $q$, i.e. it lies in $qR$.
--
--   This is Kronecker's congruence for the modular equation of prime level $q$, recorded as a divisibility relation between $\mathfrak q$-expansions inside an arbitrary subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ containing $j(\mathfrak q)$ and $j(\mathfrak q^{q})$, rather than as a congruence of polynomials. It is used in the analysis of automorphisms and integral models of modular curves at full level, where the two-chart integral model is compared with its Frobenius twist.
